From 7c179454c4e8853b1f05d0cbdd3c8f2300923c47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Wen <jackwen04@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:01:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] kk: Run the GS count pass and pre-GS program for
 transform feedback

poly lowers a GS capturing transform feedback to two more programs: a
count pass writing each input primitive's output counts, when they are not
static, and the pre-GS program, which turns their prefix sum into each
primitive's place in the buffers, advances the buffer offsets past the
draw's output and counts the transform feedback queries. Compile them
with the GS, keep them in the pipeline, and dispatch them between the
stage feeding the GS and the GS.

Without transform feedback state yet, the geometry parameters point the
buffer offsets at zeroes, so nothing fits and nothing is written, and the
counters at scratch, which the pre-GS program also gets for the pipeline
statistics KK doesn't expose. nir_ro_to_rw_poly needs no lowering on Apple
GPUs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
